      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Shepherds (Shepherd\u2019s Flock) are a cult-like group actively recruiting and agitating in the city, and they answer to the power/entity **Maelthor**.\n\nThe **Shepherd\u2019s Flock** are a protest-organizing cult operating within the city (CANON/OBSERVED). They present themselves publicly as defenders of human settlements, but internally they are engaged in recruitment and indoctrination, especially targeting \u201ctransformed\u201d individuals (CANON, OBSERVED). Their ideology frames violent or extreme acts as necessary sacrifices to \u201ccleanse\u201d the world.\n\nThey are explicitly **followers of Maelthor** (OBSERVED), and their beliefs and actions are aligned with **Maelthor\u2019s influence and emergence** (OBSERVED). This suggests a religious or quasi-religious devotion to that power, with a strong ideological bent toward **human supremacy** and purging perceived impurities (CANON).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Identity: Cult group known as the Shepherd\u2019s Flock  \n- Role: Protesters and active recruiters  \n- Allegiance: Followers of Maelthor  \n- Goals: Recruit, \u201ccleanse\u201d the world, promote human supremacy  \n- Activity: Conducting protests; hiding corrupted elements (e.g., meat); recruiting transformed individuals  \n- Public Face: Claims to defend against non-human threats  \n- True Nature: Fanatical, sacrifice-justifying cult aligned with Maelthor\u2019s influence",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
