      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the wizards; he takes the cult very seriously and pushes aggressive magical detection and containment measures.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright represents the Wizard\u2019s College on the council. He is explicitly positioned as the arcane authority and \u201cRepresentative of the Arcane\u201d (OBSERVED).\n\nHis angle on the cult is proactive and alarmed:\n- He views the corrupted meat as a perversion of magic (CANON).\n- He takes any threat to the city seriously (CANON).\n- He is eager to deploy Wizard\u2019s College resources to detect and counteract the cult\u2019s influence (OBSERVED).\n- He proposes concrete measures like a magical lockdown and rune-based detection to identify corruption (OBSERVED).\n\nIn practice, this means he advocates for decisive, system-wide magical intervention rather than cautious or political approaches.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; arcane representative (OBSERVED)\n- Goals: Magical lockdown; detection spells/runes; counter cult influence (OBSERVED)\n- Alignment/Attitude: Strongly anti-cult; sees it as a magical violation (CANON)\n- Personality: Brilliant, inventive, but can be distracted by experiments (CANON)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
