      "answer": "TL;DR: Torrin represents the Guilds (craft/industry), Rurik oversees infrastructure and city integrity, and Merril\u2019s council role is not defined in the provided context.\n\nMerril:\n- The projection contains no facts identifying Merril\u2019s role or responsibilities on the council. This is currently unknown.\n\nTorrin Flamescale:\n- CANON/OBSERVED: Representative of the Guilds; Master Smith.\n- He speaks for the craft guilds and industry, bringing a practical, blunt perspective on city issues, especially those affecting production and trade.\n\nRurik Stonehammer:\n- CANON/OBSERVED: Chief Architect; Representative of Infrastructure.\n- Responsible for the city\u2019s structural integrity, defenses, and physical layout (including tunnels and sewers), with a focus on safety and sealing vulnerabilities.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Governance:\n  - Torrin Flamescale: Guilds / craftsmanship representation.\n  - Rurik Stonehammer: Infrastructure / structural integrity.\n  - Merril: Not specified in context.\n- City Context:\n  - Council is actively deciding crisis responses (e.g., tainted meat, defenses, cult threats).",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
