      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead\u2014**Decapitated; head removed from body**\u2014with Bonogo taking the head.\n\nThe projection shows conflicting OBSERVED states: the Wolf both \u201cescapes\u201d/turns \u201cInvisible\u201d and attempts to flee via a secret passage, but also has the terminal condition **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** Because decapitation is a terminal outcome, it overrides the earlier escape attempts. Supporting this, **Bonogo\u2019s role explicitly includes \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d**\n\nSo the final, current state is: the Wolf did not ultimately get away\u2014he was killed and beheaded during or at the end of the encounter.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition (OBSERVED): **Decapitated; head removed from body** (terminal, current)\n- Operational Status (OBSERVED): Earlier escape/invisibility attempts, but superseded\n- Role in scene (CANON/OBSERVED): Central adversary in the council chamber fight\n- Related Actor: Bonogo removed and kept the head\n\nIf continuity matters: any prior \u201cfled/invisible\u201d beats occurred mid-fight, but the end state is definitively death.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
