      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence in the projection that Thalia is corrupted like the guards; her behavior appears to be directed/controlled by the Wolf, which suggests something different.\n\nFrom the available facts, the **Guards** show clear signs of corruption: \u201cAll checked guards have an oily sheen to their eyes\u201d (OBSERVED), and they interact with corrupted meat mechanically. The **Wolf** also shares this marker (\u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes\u201d) and is explicitly tied to a corrupting influence.\n\nFor **Thalia**, there is **no stated physical condition or corruption marker** in the projection. Instead, the only relevant fact is that **\u201cThe Wolf orders Thalia to attack the group\u201d** (OBSERVED). That points to external control, manipulation, or influence rather than confirmed corruption of the same type as the guards.\n\nBecause no corruption traits (like oily eyes or mechanical effects) are attributed to Thalia, the safest grounded interpretation is: **she is being compelled or influenced by the Wolf, not necessarily corrupted in the same way as the guards**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Guards (OBSERVED): oily sheen in eyes; corrupted; gain benefits near corrupted meat  \n- Wolf (OBSERVED): oily sheen in eyes; corrupting influence; issues commands  \n- Thalia (OBSERVED): ordered by the Wolf to attack; no listed corruption indicators",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_2",
