      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The chamber actively interferes via **activated runic wards, illusion magic, and environmental hazards**\u2014it can damage, disorient, and misdirect anyone not protected by council amulets.\n\nThe **Council Chambers** itself is a major combatant:\n\n- **Runic wall wards (OBSERVED):** These activate when spells are cast (e.g., Caelynn), triggering **arcane trap bursts** that can deal damage and even **temporarily paralyze** targets.\n- **Amulet-gated defenses (CANON):** Council members are marked safe, but **players without amulets may be targeted directly** by these defenses.\n- **Illusory walls (OBSERVED):** Portions of the room shift or mislead movement and sightlines, contributing to players being **disoriented by illusion spells**.\n- **Falling debris (OBSERVED):** The fight destabilizes the already **disheveled** chamber, forcing players to dodge environmental hazards.\n- **Acoustic quirks (CANON):** Voices and sounds carry unnaturally well, making stealth or coordination harder and potentially masking threats with echoing noise.\n- **Magical feedback cues (CANON):** Changes in the room\u2019s ambient hum signal when something significant (like traps) triggers.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Geography: Large circular room, high ceilings, central table, hidden trapdoor\n- Defenses: Runic wards, illusory walls, amulet-based targeting system\n- Physical Condition: Disheveled, debris hazards\n- Atmosphere: Fireball-lit, tense, sound-carrying chamber",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
