      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room shows clear signs of a chaotic, deceptive fight\u2014most notably the Wolf\u2019s **decapitated body (head removed from body)**, evidence of illusion magic, and possible disturbance near the secret passage beneath the chamber.\n\nAfter the fight, the strongest visual anchor is the Wolf\u2019s corpse: **Decapitated; head removed from body** (OBSERVED, the Wolf physical_condition). That alone tells the council this was decisive and brutal.\n\nBeyond that, the room reflects confusion and trickery rather than straightforward combat. The Wolf is known to create illusory duplicates (CANON), so you can describe lingering uncertainty\u2014scorch marks, displaced objects, or signs of \u201cattacks\u201d that may not fully line up with reality. The players were disoriented by illusions (CANON), reinforcing that the scene may feel inconsistent or uncanny.\n\nThere should also be attention drawn to the **area leading to or concealing the secret escape tunnel beneath the council chamber** (OBSERVED, the Wolf goals/operational_status). Even if not fully revealed, something about that space looks disturbed or recently used.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical condition: **Decapitated; head removed from body**\n- Magic effects: Illusory duplicates caused confusion\n- Environment: Signs of chaotic movement and misdirected attacks\n- Geography: Disturbance near hidden passage beneath the chamber",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
