      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Chambers ended Session 12 **disheveled after a Fireball lit nearly the entire room**, with **magical defenses (runes and illusory walls) actively triggered**, and **the hidden trapdoor/escape route beneath the chamber brought into play**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: **Disheveled** (OBSERVED)\n- Atmosphere Changes: \u201c**almost the entire room is lit up by Fireball**\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- Defenses Activated: **runes along the walls activated**, **illusory walls present and affecting the battle** (OBSERVED)\n- Geography Interaction: **hidden trapdoor** used as part of the Wolf\u2019s escape route beneath the chamber (OBSERVED)\n\nAdditional Outcome:\n- The confrontation culminated with the Wolf being **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (OBSERVED), marking a major turning point tied directly to the chamber scene.\n\nIn short, the room wasn\u2019t structurally destroyed, but it was heavily disrupted\u2014visually scorched by magic, magically \u0561\u056f\u057f\u056b\u057e with triggered defenses, and tactically altered by revealing/using its hidden escape infrastructure.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
