      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead at the end of Session 12\u2014**Decapitated; head removed from body**\u2014and had shown signs of corruption prior to death.\n\nThe most current **OBSERVED** physical condition includes both \u201cDecapitated\u201d and \u201chead removed from body,\u201d which are terminal outcomes and override earlier states like being invisible or escaping. While he previously had \u201can oily sheen to his eyes\u201d (a clear sign of corruption), that condition is now moot due to death.\n\nThere is no conflicting later OBSERVED state indicating survival or recovery, and Bonogo\u2019s role explicitly includes \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it,\u201d reinforcing the finality.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition (OBSERVED): Decapitated; head removed from body; previously had oily sheen to his eyes  \n- Operational Status (OBSERVED): Attempted escape earlier, but superseded by death  \n- Faction (OBSERVED): cultist  \n- Role (CANON): adversary, saboteur  \n- Mental State (OBSERVED): desperate, regretful, begging for release/killing  \n\nNet: definitively dead, formerly corrupted.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
