      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive infiltrator manipulating events; after, he is **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** and no longer an active threat, with his corruption made explicit.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy saboteur vs. neutralized target\n- Mental State: Controlled deception \u2192 desperation/regret\n- Physical Condition: Active combatant \u2192 \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d\n- Tactics: Illusions/invisibility \u2192 none (post-death)\n- Alignment Context: Hidden cult influence \u2192 visibly corrupted (oily sheen)\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED + CANON), the Wolf is a high-ranking guard (\u201csecond-in-command\u201d) and cult-aligned infiltrator who manipulates the council, creates illusory duplicates, turns invisible, and attempts escape through a secret tunnel. He actively deceives, misdirects, and even orders attacks (e.g., Thalia).\n\nDuring/after the fight (OBSERVED), that changes completely: he becomes physically overpowered and ultimately **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** His earlier subtle corruption is also made explicit via \u201can oily sheen to his eyes,\u201d and his mental state shifts to desperate and regretful (begging for release/death).\n\nSo the key shift is from cunning, hidden manipulator \u2192 exposed, corrupted, and definitively eliminated threat.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_thalia",
      "question": "Was Thalia corrupted or just played-and how does that tie to the Wolf?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
