        "not corrupted": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was **played, not corrupted**\u2014she was **ensorcelled by the Wolf**, who used that control to direct her actions.\n\nThalia shows multiple indicators of manipulation rather than corruption. She **\u201cdoes not have an oily sheen to her eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED), which is a clear marker seen in actually corrupted individuals like guards and the Wolf. Instead, she is explicitly **\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d** and even **\u201censorcelled (unbeknownst to her)\u201d** (OBSERVED). Her mental state supports this: she is noted as **\u201cInnocent\u201d**, and her **\u201cCharmed status ended\u201d**, after which she **\u201crealizes how dire the situation truly is.\u201d**\n\nThe Wolf, by contrast, is a **cultist**, a **corrupting influence**, and has **\u201can oily sheen to his eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED), tying him directly to the corruption affecting others. He also **orders Thalia to attack the group**, showing active control over her.\n\nSo the relationship is:\n- The Wolf = source of corruption and manipulation  \n- Thalia = compromised via ensorcellment, not willingly corrupted  \n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia: ensorcelled, no oily sheen, innocent, Commander of the Guard  \n- The Wolf: cultist, corrupting influence, oily sheen, deceptive and manipulative  \n- Link: direct magical control (\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d) and issued commands",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
  ],
